# Terraform
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# terraform/bootstrap uses LOCAL state on purpose (see its README) —
# never commit it even accidentally.
terraform/bootstrap/terraform.tfstate*

# Node / general
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dist/
build/
.DS_Store

# tsc's incremental/composite build-info cache — machine/run-specific,
# not deterministic source (regenerated by any `tsc`/`typecheck` run;
# apps/web's tsconfig is what currently emits this, but the pattern is
# unscoped since any package could turn on `incremental` later).
*.tsbuildinfo

# Lambda packaging build artifacts (apps/*/scripts/package-lambda.sh,
# apps/web/scripts/package-opennext.sh)
.lambda-package/
**/dist-lambda.zip
**/dist-server-lambda.zip
**/dist-image-lambda.zip
# puthagakadai.sg's own build — package-opennext.sh's optional suffix
# argument (terraform-apply.yml calls it as `package-opennext.sh sg`)
**/dist-server-lambda-sg.zip
**/dist-image-lambda-sg.zip

# apps/medusa build output (`medusa build`)
apps/medusa/.medusa/
apps/medusa/.cache/

# apps/web build output (`next build` / `open-next build`)
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/.open-next/
# terraform-apply.yml's per-storefront snapshots of .open-next/assets
# (that path is overwritten in-place by each of the two open-next
# build runs in the same job) — see that workflow's own comment.
apps/web/.open-next-assets/
apps/web/.open-next-sg-assets/
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
